[N3-A1] EXACT PIECE 1 (sympy): massless minimally coupled scalar in dS4 — retarded tail = H^2/4pi, CONSTANT inside the cone [matches BHP gr-qc/0201020 eq. 6.1 after 4pi-normalization]
====================================================================================================
  BD mode u_k = e^(-ik eta)(1 - i/(k eta))/sqrt(2k):  EOM residual = 0   Wronskian u u*' - u* u' = I
  Im[u u*'] structure check (should be 0): 0
  primitives: Int (1-cos pk)/k^2 = pi*p/2 ;  Int sin(pk)/k = pi/2
  a(eta) a(eta') eta eta' = H**(-2)  =>  TAIL of G_ret = H^2/(4 pi), constant inside the cone. [EXACT]
  cross-anchor [BHP eq. 6.1]: G_smooth = 1/C^2 = H^2 in their gauss-4pi normalization (eq. 2.10:
  box G = -4pi delta/sqrt(-g)); divide by 4pi -> H^2/4pi. Consistency: their dS mass-loss eq. 6.8
  dm/dtau = -q^2 H^2 (gauss) = -q^2 H^2/4pi (natural) = q * d/dtau[q (H^2/4pi) tau] — the SAME tail. OK

