[N3-A4] EXACT PIECE 4 (sympy): Deser-Levin worldline invariant — P(dtau) = 1 + (2H^2/k^2) sinh^2(k dtau/2), kappa = sqrt(a^2+H^2)  [DL gr-qc/9706018]
====================================================================================================
  embedding P = H^2 X.X' - target check: 0
  |a| = -H**2*r*sqrt(-1/(H**2*r**2 - 1)) ;  a^2 + H^2 = -H**2/((H*r - 1)*(H*r + 1)) = H^2/(1-H^2 r^2)
  => P(dtau) = 1 + (H^2/k^2)(cosh(k dtau) - 1) = 1 + (2H^2/k^2) sinh^2(k dtau/2), k = sqrt(a^2+H^2)  [EXACT]
     T_eff = kappa/2pi [DL]; geodesic a=0: P = cosh(H dtau) OK ; flat H->0: Rindler sinh^2 OK
  NOTE: this P(dtau; a) is what the massive tail V(P) sees -> the dissipation kernel is
  TRAJECTORY-DEPENDENT — the structure agentF's blindness lemma says is the unique bath-side escape.

