  WHY no mass evades it: the high-a tail of the dressing is (v_cone/kappa)(2 ln kappa + 1/h- + c0)
  — a (ln x)/x falloff at EVERY mass [N3-B1 correction]: the F1/Milgrom-99 LINEAR-tail class the repo
  killed at x54,000 (MI_BATH_TAIL_CONSTRAINT.md), softened only by the log. There is no exponent to tune:
  the near-cone amplitude that carries the high-a tail is H^2/4pi x (1 - m^2/2H^2) — and the dS-distinctive
  part of that cone amplitude (subtracting the flat-space massive tail -m^2/8pi) is H^2/4pi EXACTLY,
  mass-INDEPENDENT: no subtraction scheme changes the class. Past m^2 = 2H^2 the amplitude flips sign
  (anti-MOND: inertia ADDED at low a) and the channel can no longer do the galactic job at all.
